INSERT INTO cases (slug, title, domain, difficulty, category_id, company_track, estimated_minutes, scenario, instructions, supporting_data, expected_framework, model_answer, tags, is_published) VALUES (
  'comps-valuation-4', 'What Is Otter Payments Worth? A Comparables Analysis', 'finance'::domain, 'medium'::difficulty, (SELECT id FROM case_categories WHERE slug = 'valuation'), 'BCG', 40, 'Otter Payments (fintech, Southeast Asia) is preparing for a sale process. You have been asked to establish a valuation range using trading comparables.

**The company.** Revenue of **$480 M**, EBITDA margin of **23%** (EBITDA of $110 M), revenue growth of **22%**, and net debt of **$185 M**.

**Trading comparables.**

| Peer | EV/EBITDA | Revenue growth | EBITDA margin |
|---|---|---|---|
| Peer A — same sector, 3× larger | 9× | 12% | 19% |
| Peer B — adjacent sector, high growth | 10.3× | 38% | 15% |
| Peer C — same sector, declining | 7.1× | 2% | 19% |

The banker running the process has proposed simply averaging the three multiples.', 'Produce a valuation range. Provide:

1. **Analysis** — which comparables you would use and why, and the resulting enterprise and equity values.
2. **Risks** — where this methodology could mislead.
3. **Recommendation** — your valuation range and the number you would take to the seller.

Critique the banker''s proposed approach.', '{"target":{"revenue_m":480,"ebitda_margin_pct":23,"ebitda_m":110,"revenue_growth_pct":22,"net_debt_m":185},"comparables":[{"peer":"A","ev_ebitda":9,"growth_pct":12,"margin_pct":19},{"peer":"B","ev_ebitda":10.3,"growth_pct":38,"margin_pct":15},{"peer":"C","ev_ebitda":7.1,"growth_pct":2,"margin_pct":19}]}'::jsonb, '1. **Screen the peers** on growth, margin and risk — not sector label alone.
2. **Apply** the defensible multiple range to EBITDA to get enterprise value.
3. **Bridge** to equity value: EV − net debt.
4. **Adjust** for size, growth differential and marketability.
5. **Cross-check** with EV/Revenue.
6. **Present a range**, and say where in it you would settle.', '**The banker''s approach is wrong.** Averaging 9×, 10.3× and 7.1× treats three structurally different businesses as interchangeable. Peer B trades at 10.3× because it grows at 20-40%; Peer C trades at 7.1× because it is shrinking. A simple mean smuggles both distortions into the answer and produces a number with no defensible logic behind it.

**Peer screening.** Otter Payments grows at 22% with a 23% margin. Peer A is the closest analogue on sector and margin, though larger. Peer B is only relevant if this company''s growth is genuinely comparable — at 22% it arguably is. Peer C sets the floor: it is what the market pays for this sector without growth.

**Valuation.** Anchoring on Peer A at 9× and sanity-checking against the others:
- At 9×: EV = $990 M, equity = $805 M
- At 7.1× (floor): EV = $781 M, equity = $596 M
- At 10.3× (ceiling): EV = $1133 M, equity = $948 M

Note how much the net debt of $185 M matters: it moves equity value one-for-one, and it is the step most often skipped.

**Adjustments.** Apply a size discount against Peer A — smaller companies trade cheaper for liquidity and concentration reasons. In a control sale, offset this with a control premium, which typically runs 20-30%.

**Risks.** Trading comps price minority stakes in public companies on a given day; this is a control sale of a private one. Multiples also compress quickly when sentiment turns, so a range struck today has a shelf life. Three comparables is a thin sample — I would want precedent transactions as a cross-check before going to market.

**Recommendation.** A defensible range is **$596–954 M** of equity value. I would guide the seller to expect the middle of that band, and I would resist the temptation to lead with the Peer B multiple — anchoring the seller on a number the growth profile cannot support is how processes fail late and expensively.', ARRAY['comparables','multiples','ev-ebitda']::text[], true
) ON CONFLICT (slug) DO UPDATE SET
  title = EXCLUDED.title, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty,
  category_id = EXCLUDED.category_id, company_track = EXCLUDED.company_track,
  estimated_minutes = EXCLUDED.estimated_minutes, scenario = EXCLUDED.scenario,
  instructions = EXCLUDED.instructions, supporting_data = EXCLUDED.supporting_data,
  expected_framework = EXCLUDED.expected_framework, model_answer = EXCLUDED.model_answer,
  tags = EXCLUDED.tags, is_published = EXCLUDED.is_published, updated_at = now();

INSERT INTO rubrics (case_id, criteria, descriptors, max_score, pass_score) VALUES (
  (SELECT id FROM cases WHERE slug = 'comps-valuation-4'), '{"peer_selection":25,"multiple_analysis":25,"adjustments":20,"recommendation":30}'::jsonb, '{"peer_selection":"Should justify which comparables are genuinely comparable on growth, margin and risk — not just industry label.","multiple_analysis":"Expects EV/EBITDA and EV/Revenue applied correctly, with the bridge from enterprise value to equity value (subtract net debt).","adjustments":"Credit adjustments for size, growth, margin differential, liquidity and control premium.","recommendation":"A defensible valuation range with a point of view."}'::jsonb, 100, 60
) ON CONFLICT (case_id) DO UPDATE SET
  criteria = EXCLUDED.criteria, descriptors = EXCLUDED.descriptors,
