INSERT INTO cases (slug, title, domain, difficulty, category_id, company_track, estimated_minutes, scenario, instructions, supporting_data, expected_framework, model_answer, tags, is_published) VALUES (
  'comps-valuation-16', 'What Is Amber Grid Worth? A Comparables Analysis', 'finance'::domain, 'easy'::difficulty, (SELECT id FROM case_categories WHERE slug = 'valuation'), 'Goldman Sachs', 40, 'Amber Grid (utilities, Europe) is preparing for a sale process. You have been asked to establish a valuation range using trading comparables.

**The company.** Revenue of **€251 M**, EBITDA margin of **18%** (EBITDA of €45 M), revenue growth of **21%**, and net debt of **€100 M**.

**Trading comparables.**

| Peer | EV/EBITDA | Revenue growth | EBITDA margin |
|---|---|---|---|
| Peer A — same sector, 3× larger | 7.6× | 10% | 26% |
| Peer B — adjacent sector, high growth | 13.4× | 25% | 18% |
| Peer C — same sector, declining | 6.3× | -4% | 18% |

The banker running the process has proposed simply averaging the three multiples.', 'Produce a valuation range. Provide:

1. **Analysis** — which comparables you would use and why, and the resulting enterprise and equity values.
2. **Risks** — where this methodology could mislead.
3. **Recommendation** — your valuation range and the number you would take to the seller.

Critique the banker''s proposed approach.', '{"target":{"revenue_m":251,"ebitda_margin_pct":18,"ebitda_m":45,"revenue_growth_pct":21,"net_debt_m":100},"comparables":[{"peer":"A","ev_ebitda":7.6,"growth_pct":10,"margin_pct":26},{"peer":"B","ev_ebitda":13.4,"growth_pct":25,"margin_pct":18},{"peer":"C","ev_ebitda":6.3,"growth_pct":-4,"margin_pct":18}]}'::jsonb, '1. **Screen the peers** on growth, margin and risk — not sector label alone.
2. **Apply** the defensible multiple range to EBITDA to get enterprise value.
3. **Bridge** to equity value: EV − net debt.
4. **Adjust** for size, growth differential and marketability.
5. **Cross-check** with EV/Revenue.
6. **Present a range**, and say where in it you would settle.', '**The banker''s approach is wrong.** Averaging 7.6×, 13.4× and 6.3× treats three structurally different businesses as interchangeable. Peer B trades at 13.4× because it grows at 20-40%; Peer C trades at 6.3× because it is shrinking. A simple mean smuggles both distortions into the answer and produces a number with no defensible logic behind it.

**Peer screening.** Amber Grid grows at 21% with a 18% margin. Peer A is the closest analogue on sector and margin, though larger. Peer B is only relevant if this company''s growth is genuinely comparable — at 21% it arguably is. Peer C sets the floor: it is what the market pays for this sector without growth.

**Valuation.** Anchoring on Peer A at 7.6× and sanity-checking against the others:
- At 7.6×: EV = €342 M, equity = €242 M
- At 6.3× (floor): EV = €284 M, equity = €184 M
- At 13.4× (ceiling): EV = €603 M, equity = €503 M

Note how much the net debt of €100 M matters: it moves equity value one-for-one, and it is the step most often skipped.

**Adjustments.** Apply a size discount against Peer A — smaller companies trade cheaper for liquidity and concentration reasons. In a control sale, offset this with a control premium, which typically runs 20-30%.

**Risks.** Trading comps price minority stakes in public companies on a given day; this is a control sale of a private one. Multiples also compress quickly when sentiment turns, so a range struck today has a shelf life. Three comparables is a thin sample — I would want precedent transactions as a cross-check before going to market.

**Recommendation.** A defensible range is **€184–293 M** of equity value. I would guide the seller to expect the middle of that band, and I would resist the temptation to lead with the Peer B multiple — anchoring the seller on a number the growth profile cannot support is how processes fail late and expensively.', ARRAY['comparables','multiples','ev-ebitda']::text[], true
) ON CONFLICT (slug) DO UPDATE SET
  title = EXCLUDED.title, domain = EXCLUDED.domain, difficulty = EXCLUDED.difficulty,
  category_id = EXCLUDED.category_id, company_track = EXCLUDED.company_track,
  estimated_minutes = EXCLUDED.estimated_minutes, scenario = EXCLUDED.scenario,
  instructions = EXCLUDED.instructions, supporting_data = EXCLUDED.supporting_data,
  expected_framework = EXCLUDED.expected_framework, model_answer = EXCLUDED.model_answer,
  tags = EXCLUDED.tags, is_published = EXCLUDED.is_published, updated_at = now();

INSERT INTO rubrics (case_id, criteria, descriptors, max_score, pass_score) VALUES (
  (SELECT id FROM cases WHERE slug = 'comps-valuation-16'), '{"peer_selection":25,"multiple_analysis":25,"adjustments":20,"recommendation":30}'::jsonb, '{"peer_selection":"Should justify which comparables are genuinely comparable on growth, margin and risk — not just industry label.","multiple_analysis":"Expects EV/EBITDA and EV/Revenue applied correctly, with the bridge from enterprise value to equity value (subtract net debt).","adjustments":"Credit adjustments for size, growth, margin differential, liquidity and control premium.","recommendation":"A defensible valuation range with a point of view."}'::jsonb, 100, 60
) ON CONFLICT (case_id) DO UPDATE SET
  criteria = EXCLUDED.criteria, descriptors = EXCLUDED.descriptors,
